# 2. Amazon EKS Auto Mode

EKS Auto Mode simplifies Kubernetes infrastructure management.

AWS automatically manages:

* Compute
* Networking
* Storage
* Scaling
* Load balancing

Traditional EKS:

```text id="v2z8i8"
You manage:

EC2 Nodes

Node Groups

Scaling

Updates

Drivers
```

---

EKS Auto Mode:

```text id="s0z3xa"
AWS manages:

Nodes

Scaling

Storage

Networking
```

---

# 3. EKS Auto Mode Architecture

```text id="6d7z5f"
Application

    |

Kubernetes API

    |

EKS Auto Mode

    |

AWS Infrastructure

    |

Compute + Storage + Networking
```

---

# 4. Benefits of EKS Auto Mode

Advantages:

✅ Less infrastructure management
✅ Automatic scaling
✅ Simplified operations
✅ Better AWS integration
✅ Reduced maintenance effort

---

# 5. When to Use EKS Auto Mode

Good for:

* Teams new to Kubernetes
* Fast application deployment
* Standard workloads
* Reduced operational overhead

---

Not ideal for:

* Highly customized infrastructure
* Special networking requirements
* Custom node configurations

