# 6. Karpenter Introduction

Karpenter is a Kubernetes node provisioning tool.

It automatically creates EC2 nodes based on Pod requirements.

Traditional scaling:

```text id="9md6jc"
Pod Pending

↓

Cluster Autoscaler

↓

Increase Node Group Size

↓

New Node
```

---

Karpenter:

```text id="f5kq3r"
Pod Pending

↓

Karpenter

↓

Select Best EC2 Instance

↓

Create Node
```

---

# 7. Karpenter Architecture

```text id="8b8m4w"
              Kubernetes Scheduler

                       |

                  Pending Pods

                       |

                    Karpenter

                       |

              EC2 Instance Selection

                       |

                  New Worker Node
```

---

# 8. Karpenter Benefits

Advantages:

* Faster scaling
* Better instance selection
* Lower cost
* Automatic node lifecycle management

---

Example:

Application requires:

```text id="6f4q5n"
CPU: 16 cores

Memory: 64GB
```

Karpenter selects:

```text id="j7t6u4"
Suitable EC2 Instance
```

---

# 9. Karpenter NodePool Concept

NodePool defines:

* Instance types
* Capacity type
* Architecture
* Limits

Example:

```yaml id="m8z5cw"
apiVersion: karpenter.sh/v1

kind: NodePool

spec:

 requirements:

 - key: kubernetes.io/arch

   operator: In

   values:

   - amd64
```

---

# 10. Karpenter vs Cluster Autoscaler

| Feature            | Karpenter | Cluster Autoscaler |
| ------------------ | --------- | ------------------ |
| Scaling            | Pod based | Node group based   |
| Speed              | Faster    | Slower             |
| Instance selection | Dynamic   | Fixed              |
| Cost optimization  | Better    | Limited            |
| AWS integration    | Strong    | Standard           |

