# 22. Node Labels

Labels describe nodes.

Example:

```text id="6n0s4k"
Node 1

label:

gpu=true


Node 2

label:

gpu=false
```

---

# 23. Node Selector

Simple scheduling rule.

Example:

Run Pod only on GPU nodes:

```yaml id="n6p1qm"
nodeSelector:

 gpu: "true"
```

---

# 24. Node Affinity

Advanced node selection.

Example:

Prefer:

```text id="x9j3dk"
Run application on:

High-memory nodes
```

---

Example:

```yaml id="d8f3zc"
affinity:

 nodeAffinity:

  requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
```

---

# 25. Pod Affinity

Places Pods together.

Example:

Frontend and cache:

```text id="a7n8kp"
Node 1

Frontend

Redis
```

Useful when:

* Low latency is required

---

# 26. Pod Anti-Affinity

Separates Pods.

Example:

```text id="r4m8yx"
Node A

Application Pod


Node B

Application Pod
```

Benefits:

* High availability
* Failure protection

---

# 27. Taints and Tolerations

Used to control which Pods run on nodes.

Example:

GPU node:

```text id="q5m8zs"
Node

Taint:

GPU=true
```

Only Pods with tolerance can run.

---

Pod:

```yaml id="8h6t8x"
tolerations:

- key: GPU

  effect: NoSchedule
```

